-- title:
--   Level H² classes over open subgroups of G_{ℚ_q} die in an unramified layer
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ and $q$ be primes, and let $\mathrm{primeLocalGaloisGroup}\ q$ denote the group of $\mathbb{Q}_q$-algebra automorphisms of the algebraic closure $\mathrm{PadicAlgCl}\ q$ of $\mathbb{Q}_q$, equipped with the homomorphism `primeLocalToGlobal q` to $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ obtained by restricting scalars to $\mathbb{Q}$ and then restricting to the normal subextension $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $S$ be a subgroup of $\mathrm{primeLocalGaloisGroup}\ q$ such that, for some intermediate field $F_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}$, the preimage under `primeLocalToGlobal q` of the fixing subgroup of $F_0$ is contained in $S$. Let $B$ be a representation of $S$ over $\mathbb{Z}/p$, finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Z}/p$, which is smooth in the sense that every $b \in B$ admits an intermediate field $F$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$, finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}$, such that every $s \in S$ whose image under `primeLocalToGlobal q` lies in the fixing subgroup of $F$ acts trivially on $b$. Let $b : S \times S \to B$ lie in `levelCocycles₂` for the homomorphism $S \hookrightarrow \mathrm{primeLocalGaloisGroup}\ q \to \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ and the representation $B$. Then there is an $N > 0$ such that the restriction of $b$ to $S \sqcap T_N$, where $T_N$ is the fixing subgroup of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ adjoined with all $\zeta \in \mathrm{PadicAlgCl}\ q$ satisfying $\zeta^{q^N - 1} = 1$, lies in `levelCoboundaries₂` for the corresponding homomorphism precomposed with the inclusion $S \sqcap T_N \le S$ and the restricted representation `Rep.res` of $B$.
--
--   In finite-level form this is the statement that $p$-cohomological dimension considerations make every continuous degree-two class over an open subgroup of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q/\mathbb{Q}_q)$ vanish after passing to the unramified layer generated by the $(q^N-1)$-st roots of unity, $N$ large. It feeds the right-exactness of continuous $H^2$ for such subgroups and is cited by [`groupCohomology.exists_restrict_comap_rootsOfUnity_mem_levelCoboundaries2_of_primeLocal`](thm.html#groupCohomology.exists_restrict_comap_rootsOfUnity_mem_levelCoboundaries2_of_primeLocal).
-- source:
